 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412058 1080 "II and III only" 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412058 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412058 1083 #uuid "dbd590b8-7f9d-5cdd-9e3e-23772a325ceb" 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412059 1080 "I and III only" 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412059 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412059 1083 #uuid "e04a3a05-fb55-5020-b5ef-f2fc7abaa120" 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412060 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412055 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412060 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412056 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412060 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412057 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412060 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412058 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412060 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412059 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412060 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412060 1077 "selection" 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412060 1078 #edb/ref 17592186412057 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412060 1079 #uuid "11a0d3a7-d6ab-5c8b-9be2-dd9dc9a08b2a" 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412061 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412060 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412061 1069 "q-42481" 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412061 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412061 1071 "Given that $det(A)=14$, and $I$ is the $3\\times 3$ identity matrix, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\text{det}(A)-\\text{det}(3I)=-13$\n- $-\\text{det}({A}^{T})+\\text{det}(I)=-13$\n- $\\text{det}(A)-\\text{det}({A}^{T})=-28$" 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412061 1072 #uuid "03fcc7d2-8c99-53e1-b5b5-d7a0f5cd296f" 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412061 1074 "From the properties of determinants, we know that \n\n$$\n\\text{det}({A}^{T})=\\text{det}(A)=14\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ndet(I)=1.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3I & =3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a diagonal matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| & ={3}^{3}=27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\text{det}(A)-\\text{det}(3I)=14-27=-13\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n-\\text{det}({A}^{T})+\\text{det}(I)=-14+1=-13\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\text{det}(A)-\\text{det}({A}^{T})=14-14=0\\ne -28\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412062 1058 #edb/ref 17592186412065 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412062 1062 #uuid "01ba53dd-2af4-5943-b33a-3f9957a64861" 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412062 1063 #edb/ref 17592186370953 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412063 1058 #edb/ref 17592186412064 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412063 1062 #uuid "12dce7a0-7e88-5278-b9ed-ee4ec2da47a3" 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412063 1063 #edb/ref 17592186265895 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412064 1062 #uuid "1de5148a-4da4-5b0e-a636-e0a0b5edb677" 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412064 1063 #edb/ref 17592186275470 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412065 1058 #edb/ref 17592186412063 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412065 1062 #uuid "df91f40e-b959-5674-99bf-2ff407d8aa6f" 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412065 1063 #edb/ref 17592186338734 13194139534144 17592186045417 true] [17592186412066 1058 #edb/ref 17592186412062 1319413